{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "In overlapping treatment categories, Kainuu's crude curative share is 20.8% (95% CI 16.0–26.6) versus 27.0% nationally, and crude life-prolonging share is 18.6% (95% CI 14.1–24.2) versus 30.4%.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:curative:Kainuun_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:curative",
        "cty:life_prolonging:Kainuun_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:life_prolonging"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Treatment categories overlap because a patient can receive multiple treatments; Kainuu's crude curative share is 20.8% (95% CI 16.0–26.6; n=47/226) versus 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally, and its crude life-prolonging share is 18.6% (95% CI 14.1–24.2; n=42/226) versus 30.4% (4522/14873) nationally, with each 95% confidence interval excluding the national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Kainuun_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Kainuun_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Kainuu's crude symptomatic treatment share is 48.2% (95% CI 41.8–54.7; n=109/226), where the 95% confidence interval excludes the national value of 39.5% (5871/14873) in these overlapping treatment categories.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:symptomatic:Kainuun_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The crude share of patients with no treatment record within 12 months is 28.3% (95% CI 22.9–34.5; n=64/226) versus 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally, with the 95% confidence interval including the national value; this category mixes untreated patients and unrecorded treatment.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Kainuun_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A multidisciplinary team (MDT) meeting is recorded for a crude share of 0.9% (95% CI 0.2–3.2; n=2/226) of Kainuu patients, with the 95% confidence interval excluding the national value of 6.0% (893/14873), though MDT records measure recording practice rather than care because procedures enter HILMO only from direct patient contacts.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Kainuun_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Diagnosis concordance is high, but county treatment shares are crude, neither age-adjusted nor stage-adjusted, and public data omit pathway timestamps and primary care visits.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "lit:hilmo_90",
        "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "A journal article found HILMO diagnoses match the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types (diagnosis concordance only), whereas Taulukko 11 gives only crude, unadjusted county shares; age-adjusted curative shares appear only in Kuva 16, with digitised (±0.5 percentage points) national reference lines of 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "lit:hilmo_90",
          "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Separately from age adjustment, county treatment shares are crude and cannot be stage-adjusted because stage at diagnosis is missing for about 48% of new patients, and Finland currently has no cancer quality registry, so lung cancer data reporting, collection and storage remain incomplete.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "filha:registry",
          "q:47c7e11303",
          "q:950a2f797b"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Primary care visits are not included in the report's data and occupational health is not mentioned; public data also lack symptom onset, referral dates, imaging waits (showing only that about 20% of diagnoses rely on clinical examination such as imaging alone), and visit or treatment start dates, though 93.6% have a specialist visit within 12 months.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Preliminary, unpublished national figures—not county-specific data—indicate that lung cancer care in Finland takes 155 days on average from symptoms to treatment (56 days patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care, the longest stage), compared with 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends reporting THL 21/2016 access times with handover alerts, adopting a KYS-style referral template, persistent-symptoms rule and diagnostic contact, and publishing coding data.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "thl:21_2016",
        "q:82d365cd2c"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The team recommends reporting access times using THL Ohjaus 21/2016 definitions (16 cancers) and flagging stalled handovers: the Health Care Act (§52) sets no maximum time for cancer suspicion, the STM roadmap (measure 3.1.2) plans national pathways with access times by 2026–2028, and the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation is to be carried out before the 2030 mid-term evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "law:no_max",
          "q:ed87906241",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:b326e35410",
          "q:432c0e51d6",
          "q:614febebf2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends adopting a KYS-style referral template, a rule referring persistent symptoms despite a normal X-ray to a pulmonologist, and a diagnostic-phase contact person: mentor insight notes weak referrals get lower urgency ratings, KYS's pathway document provides the template and X-ray rule, and the STM roadmap plans referral criteria (measure 2.5.2) and coordinator guidance (measure 1.2.3) by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:kys_template",
          "reg:kys_persistent",
          "reg:named_contact",
          "q:37bb4c3b38",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:050ee09ebe",
          "q:abcbb06ae3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends publishing per county how completely stage, drug treatment and MDT meetings are recorded as data-quality signals, given Kainuu's crude 0.9% (95% CI 0.2–3.2; n=2/226) MDT recording (95% CI excluding 6.0% nationally) and about 48% missing stage, while the STM roadmap (measure 3.2.1) plans a quality registry with a 90% coverage indicator (decree by 2026–2028, reports by 2029–2031).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Kainuun_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695",
          "q:f540c706f8"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
